; FILED: (tensor <rectangular nested collection>) — NATIVE is the wrong side.
; The VM now builds the rank-N tensor the nesting describes; native flattens the
; outer level and zero-fills.
; native -r : #(0 0)              shape (2)
; vm        : #((1 2) (3 4))      shape (2 2)
; The VM also rejects a ragged nesting rather than truncating it. Gate the
; nested form in corpus/39_tensor_constructor.esk once the native constructor
; lands; every VARIADIC form of (tensor ...) already agrees and is gated there.
(display (tensor (list (list 1.0 2.0) (list 3.0 4.0))))
(newline)
(display (tensor-shape (tensor (list (list 1.0 2.0) (list 3.0 4.0)))))
(newline)
